# Supabase (Optional - remove if not using backend)
#
# IMPORTANT: put your TEST environment keys here, never your live keys.
# This file feeds local `npm run dev` — it must never touch real user data.
# Which keys go here depends on the Environment strategy chosen in /init
# (see docs/PRD.md → Constraints):
#   - local         → your LOCAL Supabase instance (from `supabase start`),
#                     e.g. URL http://127.0.0.1:54321 and the local anon key
#                     it prints. Production is migrated at /deploy.
#   - two-projects  → your "dev" project's keys (the "prod" project's keys
#                     are added in the host's panel at /deploy, never here)
#   - single        → your one project's keys (test == live; be careful)
#   - branching     → your persistent "staging" branch keys (production is
#                     promoted via Merge at /deploy)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_url_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Add more environment variables as needed
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_...
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.sendgrid.net
# SMTP_USER=your_smtp_user
# SMTP_PASS=your_smtp_password
